020-b85720b98174": {"__data__": {"id_": "1bac279e-b79d-426e-a020-b85720b98174", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"id": "phishing_10", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Quishing (QR Code Phishing)", "lang": "en"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "cf511d41-4ff6-40ac-b35a-a834adc6e433", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"id": "phishing_10", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Quishing (QR Code Phishing)", "lang": "en"}, "hash": "c3b4b96592efb58116fce365a04f0e5d86f254b7f362d0502c9d90881820685b", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "In quishing, attackers exploit QR codes to redirect users to fraudulent sites.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 78, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, "93561e15-b0be-4d1b-8162-c0da03f4f8e4": {"__data__": {"id_": "93561e15-b0be-4d1b-8162-c0da03f4f8e4", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"id": "phishing_11", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Quishing (QR Code Phishing)", "lang": "en"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "47237390-d8cb-452e-99ba-07335c3fe2b0", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"id": "phishing_11", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Quishing (QR Code Phishing)", "lang": "en"}, "hash": "bcab56c6464f4fe5e44b99bbc4e22f33d5d62f216ffec7f156e007281d042b38", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "This is often tied to fake emails about undelivered shipments or failed payments.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 81, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, "988e54a9-308a-4d72-8c25-fa1fed582708": {"__data__": {"id_": "988e54a9-308a-4d72-8c25-fa1fed582708", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"id": "phishing_12", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Quishing (QR Code Phishing)", "lang": "en"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "20d68247-6373-45b4-a04d-fd5969225be0", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"id": "phishing_12", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Quishing (QR Code Phishing)", "lang": "en"}, "hash": "5363440d4bc5035a9c3930cf681ec38b2b1b9313ae013410160259d60647cc1a", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Scenario:\n- Victims scan a QR code believing it to be from a trusted source and are led to input their credit card and personal details on malicious websites.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 158, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, "2ee6d9b3-0eb9-4908-b54c-42e0252c6556": {"__data__": {"id_": "2ee6d9b3-0eb9-4908-b54c-42e0252c6556", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"id": "phishing_13", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "SIM Swapping", "lang": "en"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "622077a1-db46-4fea-8f94-833de4d218bc", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"id": "phishing_13", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "SIM Swapping", "lang": "en"}, "hash": "1885b7871b91ad20245794d63bfaa5d359b8422c0572fc9842c3e563e5b659c0", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Attackers take control of a victim\u2019s phone number by fraudulently requesting a SIM replacement from telecom providers using fake IDs.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 133, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, "d33992a2-c5f8-4afb-805d-640bd09e8128": {"__data__": {"id_": "d33992a2-c5f8-4afb-805d-640bd09e8128", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"id": "phishing_14", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "SIM Swapping", "lang": "en"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "f4d83fd8-43aa-4491-91c8-ff8e6dbb723f", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"id": "phishing_14", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "SIM Swapping", "lang": "en"}, "hash": "f4d2f12920427d6f355a76c013527f7624a8be64934032d60a5a0a4b3b033c94", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "\n", "text": "Scenario:\n- Once the new SIM is activated, attackers intercept calls and SMS (including OTPs), gaining unauthorized access to bank accounts and sensitive apps.", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 0, "end_char_idx": 159, "metadata_seperator": "\n", "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, "f997615b-d7e7-4dd4-8d75-cdb0c2a10e42": {"__data__": {"id_": "f997615b-d7e7-4dd4-8d75-cdb0c2a10e42", "embedding": null, "metadata": {"id": "phishing_15", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Social Media Phishing", "lang": "en"}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {"1": {"node_id": "34ff39a6-acc3-43c3-aa1e-dd9b328a1d91", "node_type": "4", "metadata": {"id": "phishing_15", "source": "Phishing Scenarios", "doc_type": "explainer", "title": "Social Media Phishing", "lang": "en"}, "hash": "1fe8e163a88189cfd111305ad520f1c79853d6529e9a30847a2a3cf1631b6ae1", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "metadata_template": "{